<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><span id="S4.T3.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantitative Evaluation for Indoor 3D Scene Generation</span> on the synthetic 3D-FRONT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> dataset. The best results for each metric are in <span id="S4.T3.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>; second-best are <span id="S4.T3.21" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>. We report metrics on <span id="S4.T3.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">small-scale scenes</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> of <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m\times 2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m\times 2m</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
